{"availability":"available","full":"aniruddhaadak80/noema","name":"noema","description":"An interactive atlas of the human brain and mind — 31 regions, 12 neurotransmitters, 7 networks, 24 philosophy positions, and an honest comparison against AI. Next.js 16.","category":"Design","language":"TypeScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-10T04:25:12Z","updated":"2026-10-11T22:53:55Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://noema-atlas.vercel.app","topics":["anatomy","brain","cognitive-science","consciousness","interactive-atlas","neuroscience","nextjs","open-source","philosophy-of-mind","psychology","tailwindcss","turbopack","vercel"],"demo":"https://noema-atlas.vercel.app/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T07:59:38.849Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-12T07:59:38.849Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-12T07:59:38.849Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-12T07:59:38.849Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Next.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["An interactive atlas of the human brain and mind. 31 cortical and subcortical regions, 12 neurotransmitters, 7 large-scale networks, 14 landmark experiments, 12 cognitive biases, 24 positions on the philosophy of mind, 5 thought experiments, and an honest comparison against a 2026 frontier AI model — every figure with its source and its dispute.","Everyone knows the brain has 86 billion neurons. Almost nobody knows that the figure comes from four brains, that the sample data were never published, that the 95% confidence interval on that mean spans roughly 73 to 99 billion, and that a second study of five older women came back with 61–73 billion — a range that does not overlap.","Nine whole human brains have ever been counted by isotropic fractionation. Everything else in neuroscience is inference from partial data, metaphor, and a century of careful work on things that turn out to be shakier than their reputations."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/aniruddhaadak80/noema/blob